# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-21). L §3.6: "No rule is a refusal. An arrival the rule doesn't reach is a def with
# no rule that applies (RUN-NO-RULE, §5.11): missing law is never a hole and never a default." wage is a transfer, and
# the rule reaches only wages.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
kind wages: transfers
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0 when m in wages
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-01-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (refused: RUN-NO-RULE no rule applies to arrive[wage, ania] on 2026-02-01, 0.00 PLN, refused: RUN-NO-RULE no rule applies to arrive[wage, ania] on 2026-02-01)
  cut 2026-01-01
